Supersedes the unmerged a613f36bc7, split and reworked per coordinator
directive after a hostile same-day review (12 findings; details in the
spec amendment and the design note's appended section).

The mechanism: the loop's dispatch layer used to refuse unknown tool
calls and keep only a conflated counter (tool_call_parse_failures mixes
unknown names with malformed JSON; 8 live rows carry it with no
recoverable kind). Now the demanded IDENTITY survives — unknown_tool and
bad_arguments events on the session, plus loose-extracted names from
tool-call text both strict transports refuse — and rides the stats into
harness rows, the repair record, AND the primary live induction's
attempt["tool_gap"]. New tools enter as HUMAN-AUTHORED candidates via
register_candidate_tool behind CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_CANDIDATE_TOOLS,
frozen per session, byte-identical when unset. The offline analyzer
(scripts/arc_tool_gap_refine.py) keeps a durable ledger and emits
human-only specifications in the ops/verifier_gaps.md convention; it
never generates a tool.

Review findings fixed here (owned per the Error Lifecycle):
- F2 (premise-level): as first built, NO env configuration let the live
  agent both run the loop and record gap events — the loop runs under
  CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP "1"/"selfparse" and the only widened
  record was on the mutually-exclusive "repair" branch. The primary
  induce site now pre-clears the diagnostic and copies gap fields onto
  the attempt; the stale-stats direction is pinned.
- F3/F4: an unknown name with unparseable arguments was discarded
  although the name needed no parse; unparsed tool-call text on either
  transport held the demanded name and only a counter moved. Both
  populations are captured now.
- F5/F7: candidate enablement is frozen at session creation — payload,
  prompt, dispatch, and the record read one snapshot; the cross-run
  limit of the human-only boundary is disclosed in the spec instead of
  asserted (in-process model-executed code can mutate the registry, and
  no in-process guard survives that threat model).
- F6/F9: a registered-but-dark candidate no longer alters XML coercion;
  model-controlled event strings are capped before the durable ledger.
- F8 corrigendum: the first cut claimed "Zero decorative rules" and the
  review falsified it three ways (dropped-counter finalize proven only
  at the session attribute, a tautological markdown assertion, refusal
  text unbound from the active set). All three now have biting tests.
- F10: the gap doc's no-demand null was over-generalized as "live"; the
  corpus is entirely the server-lifted transport (selfparse_blocks_seen
  0 throughout). Corrected append-style in ops/arc_tool_gaps.md.

Mutation record, re-run in full after the fixes: 26 feature mutation runs
(labels M1-M14 refreshed post-refactor, M17-M24 with M22 in two halves, M27-M28), each RED, each
restore byte-identical. The freshness-lint rider's M15/M16/M25/M26 live
in its own commit.

Not merged to main; branch worktree-agent-a092d79bdf0704db3 only, per
coordinator hold.

